# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles" (the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else), and the transcript sem-ch07-flatten-held derives for the same lines in the other order (ruling FV): the inc moves the inner `$a` in its tick; the swap fires the outer at 2, the flatten adopts `$b` after 2 and reads 101 at 3. Only the positions differ: the label is 0, the buttons 1 and 2.
test the_flatten_follows_and_adopts

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="0")
    1: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    2: Ui.Button(label="swap")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    0: Ui.Label(text="1")

tick 2
  in:
    2: click

tick 3
  changed:
    0: Ui.Label(text="101")
